I never saw the previous suggestion but I like this idea.

Although it does seem sort of strange if there is more than
one co-aligned altar.. "Ah so you have found my mintetown
altar! Here's another artifact for talking in my other ear!"

Perhaps an altar that is generated co-aligned can only get you
the first gift (meaning there is no difference between
there being one or four of them), and cross-aligned altars
can each give you an extra?  So if your only altar is cross-
aligned, you can get two artifacts for it--but only one
if you've already claimed your "first gift" from some other
altar.

To me this makes sense; your god has one artifact set aside
as your general right and further artifacts are given as
rewards for converting altars (which I assume pleases the
god in question).

